course: dictionary
lesson: 6936
title: Pagan
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A pagan was a person who followed an old religion with many gods and goddesses, before Christianity or Islam spread. The Romans, Anglo-Saxons and Vikings all had pagan religions. As an adjective, pagan describes things from those times, such as «pagan gods» or «pagan festivals».
explain: Look at the context: «Volodymyr was not a saint from the start: as a young pagan prince he fought his own brothers for the throne.» The words «not a saint from the start» and «fought his own brothers» tell you he was a different person before his change. The clue is that a pagan prince followed the old gods, not the Christian faith.
explain: Today, a Pagan with a capital P follows a modern nature-based religion, such as Wicca or Druidry. In the past, some people used «pagan» to mean anyone who was not Christian, Jewish or Muslim. That use is old and often unkind, so do not use it that way yourself.
fact: Pagan means following an old religion with many gods and goddesses.
fact: Anglo-Saxons and Vikings were pagans who worshipped gods such as Woden (Odin) and Thor.
fact: Wednesday means Woden's day, and Thursday means Thor's day.
fact: Some Christian festivals took over pagan customs, such as Yule and Easter eggs.
fact: Today, a Pagan follows a modern nature-based religion, such as Wicca or Druidry.
exercise: «Before his baptism Volodymyr was a fierce pagan prince.» Before his baptism, what was Volodymyr? | A village farmer | *A pagan prince | A Christian saint | A teacher
exercise: In history lessons, what does pagan mean? | A person who only reads history books | A person who lives by the sea | *A person who followed an old religion with many gods | A person who builds churches
exercise: Which day is named after Thor, a pagan god? | Monday | Saturday | *Thursday | Tuesday
test: «Afterwards he built churches and schools, and the Church later made him a saint.» What does this show about Volodymyr's life? | He never changed at all | *He changed from a pagan prince into a Christian who built churches | He hated building things | He was a Viking from the start
test: Which custom did some Christian festivals take over from pagan times? | Monday assemblies | Reading library books | Playing football | *Easter eggs
exam: Today, what does a Pagan with a capital P usually follow? | Only the rules of school | *A modern nature-based religion, such as Wicca or Druidry | A religion that began in Rome | A daily newspaper
